{"chunk_id": "de2bcd93e90c", "text": "Duryodhana secretly attempts to murder Bhima by mixing powerful poison into food and feeding it to him under the guise of friendship. After the princes finish playing in the water, the poison overwhelms Bhima; while he lies unconscious, Duryodhana binds him with creepers and throws him into the river. Bhima sinks into the realm of the Nagas (serpents), who bite him repeatedly\u2014yet their venom counteracts the poison in his blood. When he awakens, he overpowers the snakes, but they bring their king Vasuki, who recognizes Bhima as kin through Aryaka. Welcomed and honored, Bhima drinks eight jars of a divine nectar that grants immense strength. Meanwhile, in Hastinapura, the others return without him. Kunti and Yudhishthira fear the worst, while Vidura counsels silence and faith that Bhima will return.\nDuryodhana poisons and drowns Bhima, but snake venom revives him in the Naga realm where he drinks nectar granting immense strength.\nThemes: treachery, divine protection, family rivalry, supernatural aid, power transformation", "vector": [0.010019710287451744, -0.01376615185290575, -0.0031534796580672264, 0.015012719668447971, -0.017842765897512436, 0.023098565638065338, -0.025322172790765762, -0.011057393625378609, -0.006829170510172844, -0.023314187303185463, 0.006121658720076084, -0.006263161078095436, 0.014244564808905125, 0.0032680293079465628, -0.008220609277486801, 0.005629769992083311, 0.0529622882604599, -0.003219177247956395, 0.04247764125466347, -0.029324667528271675, -0.0019136500777676702, 0.0032276001293212175, 0.022640367969870567, 0.03681755065917969, -0.032747674733400345, 0.021306203678250313, 0.007351381238549948, -0.038407765328884125, 0.01878611370921135, -0.004117043223232031, 0.0057106283493340015, -0.007627647835761309, 0.003402793314307928, 0.003908158745616674, -0.020376330241560936, 0.008611425757408142, -0.005818439647555351, -0.018705256283283234, 0.008348635397851467, -0.01388070173561573, 0.0075333